        "node_id": "n_9_3f08d0",
        "thought_text": "Iterate starting from $k=1$, accumulating the sum $S = k(k+1)/2$ and checking if $S \\ge d$ and $(S - d) \\pmod 2 == 0$. Stop immediately when both conditions are met. This is $O(\\sqrt{d})$ which is efficient enough for $d \\le 10^9$.",
