        "thought_text": "Calculate the absolute difference $d = |a - b|$. Find the smallest integer $k$ such that the sum of integers from 1 to $k$ (which is $k(k+1)/2$) is at least $d$. Then, if the difference between this sum and $d$ is odd, increment $k$ by 1 to make the difference even, ensuring the remaining value can be distributed to balance the numbers.",
