        "thought_text": "Use binary search to find the minimum $k$ where $k(k+1)/2 eq d$. Once a candidate $k$ is found, check the parity of the remainder. If the remainder is odd, the answer is $k+1$; otherwise, it is $k$. This avoids direct square root calculations and floating-point issues.",
